# Local Network Publishing

After completing user-requested application changes:

1. Run the relevant backend and frontend checks.
2. If checks pass, run `powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/publish-kronos-lan.ps1 -SkipChecks`.
3. Confirm both the frontend and proxied API health endpoint respond at the canonical LAN URL.
4. Include this local-network URL in the final handoff (always):

   **http://192.168.86.197:5173/**

Do not publish broken builds. Documentation-only changes do not require republishing.
The backend stays on loopback; LAN clients access it through the frontend proxy.

Publish must run on the Windows host that owns `192.168.86.197`. Cloud agent VMs
cannot serve that address; if publish is requested from a cloud agent, update the
scripts/config as needed and tell the user to run the publish script on that host
(or use a self-hosted Cursor worker on it).
